{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cevt3mXWbtkGzTW1RDfpr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build was red because `patchy`'s source-patching code never registered patched functions' source with `linecache`, and every patched function shared the literal filename `\"<patchy>\"`. That broke `inspect.getsource`/`pdb`/traceback support for patched functions — three real tests were catching a real gap in functionality, not flakiness.\n\nFix in `src/patchy/api.py`:\n- Each patched function now gets a unique synthetic filename (`<patchy {qualname}-{n}>`) instead of the shared literal `\"<patchy>\"`.\n- After swapping in the new code object, its source is registered in `linecache.cache` with `mtime=None`, marking it as a loader-backed entry `linecache.checkcache()` won't evict.\n\n`python -m pytest` now reports `59 passed, 1 xfailed` (the xfail was already there before my changes, unrelated). I deliberately didn't touch or skip the three failing tests — deleting them would have hidden this gap rather than fixed it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":44294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1270},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c165cf13-730b-48da-ac4a-731c0f8b0b4d","uuid":"e3a03173-0e7f-4d60-993d-e91998972295","timestamp":"2026-09-11T02:41:56.242Z","request_id":"req_011Cevt3m4irak6U5fF8LvRY"}
